    {
      "album": "Around Here, The Birds Plant The Trees",
      "artist": "Natalia Beylis",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/around-here-the-birds-plant-the-trees",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "modern classical / ambient",
      "excerpt": "Ambient composer Natalia Beylis leads an ensemble of Nyahh’s finest in her landscape-shaped evocation of a field in Leitrim, Éire, quietly meditating on the natural logic of birds and trees. ‘Around Here The Birds Plant The Trees’ is Beylis’ slow-burn, long-form arrangement for quintet - Eimear Reidy (cello), Tola Custy (fiddle), Ailbhe Nic Oireachtaigh & Ultan O’Brien (violin), and Willie Stewart (percussion) - seeded in her reading of a blackbird’s dawn chorus, and subsequent conversation with",
      "body": "Ambient composer Natalia Beylis leads an ensemble of Nyahh’s finest in her landscape-shaped evocation of a field in Leitrim, Éire, quietly meditating on the natural logic of birds and trees.\n\n‘Around Here The Birds Plant The Trees’ is Beylis’ slow-burn, long-form arrangement for quintet - Eimear Reidy (cello), Tola Custy (fiddle), Ailbhe Nic Oireachtaigh & Ultan O’Brien (violin), and Willie Stewart (percussion) - seeded in her reading of a blackbird’s dawn chorus, and subsequent conversation with a local farmer on how “birds are the architects of the living landscape”. It follows some 40 solo albums over the past 20 years (not to mention jams with Woven Skull and Tomuttontu) with a considered approach to what lies just beyond her home; typically drawing on her attentive reading of the rural soundsphere to transmute the poetry of birdsong and the natural world into expressive musical metaphor.\n\nThe low bowed cello tone of regular spar Eimear Reidy underlines and opens out a breezy space where where the fiddle and violinists criss-cross air in reserved melodic flight and plucky figures that alternate like the play of light on Ireland’s remote North West. The piece unfolds to boggy pockets of percussion and passages of barely-there, hushed gloam, as though the wind itself was generating the players’ gestures, which rise to cloud castle hover around the midway, only to depart for Nyahh label boss Willie Stewart’s rolling drum thunder and scrape of Ailbhe Nic Oireachtaigh's fiddle rooted in the rolling landscape. Ultimately the folk soul of the turf rises in its final section, resembling a rousing, swaying folk song voiced by the strings in ideally creaky discord.",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "Lovely Dave",
      "artist": "Lovely Dave",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/lovely-dave",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "electronic",
      "excerpt": "The eminently watchable Accidental Meetings introduce extended family member, Lovely Dave, with a real guess-again mixtape (the first in a series) refracting myriad strains of blissed synths, outernational jazz, new wave pop, post punk scuzz, screwed club and dub Six years into Accidental Meetings’ serendipitous plot, we know to expect anything and everything from the Bristol label, so long as it's got a unique soul and does not bore. Lovely Dave ideally plays true to that brief on his 99 minute",
      "body": "The eminently watchable Accidental Meetings introduce extended family member, Lovely Dave, with a real guess-again mixtape (the first in a series) refracting myriad strains of blissed synths, outernational jazz, new wave pop, post punk scuzz, screwed club and dub\n\nSix years into Accidental Meetings’ serendipitous plot, we know to expect anything and everything from the Bristol label, so long as it's got a unique soul and does not bore. Lovely Dave ideally plays true to that brief on his 99 minute mixtape, effortlessly glyding from outernational synth folk to a killer Curtis Mayfield cover via everything from thumb piano meditations, jazz-funked sidewinders, and a proto-new beat bomb on the A-side, before swerving from gothic new wave to smudged minimal wave audities, a pitch-slapped batacuda house ace, and meter-messing skronk on the backside.\n\nBrilliantly strange but true!",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "AMERICAN DUB ELECTRONICS",
      "artist": "Various Artists",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/american-dub-electronics",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "basic channel / dub techno",
      "excerpt": "A quiet show of strength from Chicago’s budding and already highly sought after Dub Techno specialists, Kino Disk, hustling 11 exclusive permutations of dub-suffixed ambient, techno, and elemental abstraction by label regulars and new figures including Eustress, Infant, 8004 and many others, huge tip FFO Chain Reaction, Huerco S., Echospace, Short Span, Vialan. In the space of 20 odd releases since 2024, Kino Disk has emerged as a key point of interest for off-grid dub aficionados. ‘American Dub",
      "body": "A quiet show of strength from Chicago’s budding and already highly sought after Dub Techno specialists, Kino Disk, hustling 11 exclusive permutations of dub-suffixed ambient, techno, and elemental abstraction by label regulars and new figures including Eustress, Infant, 8004 and many others, huge tip FFO Chain Reaction, Huerco S., Echospace, Short Span, Vialan.\n\nIn the space of 20 odd releases since 2024, Kino Disk has emerged as a key point of interest for off-grid dub aficionados. ‘American Dub Electronics’ now opens an ideal entry portal to their microcosm, rendering 11 exclusive bits that speak to the label’s fine grasp of variation within a theme. Trust it’s not wall-to-wall mark & moritz worship, rather a webbed spectra of interrelated, American POV’s on the same gauzy spirit from their collected vapours.\n\nBuilding on the smouldering embers of over 30 years of precedents in this field, the set sways from the moonlit tidal movement of Psalm Star Electric’s ‘001’ to the unmoored slosh of 8006 (whose ‘8004’ was a sleeper gem of ’25) with a particularly nocturnal appeal. Eustress practices the most Catholic form of dub house in the darkly luminous ‘mm’, and Eden Aurelius’ Ring impress with the ASMR-like sensitivities of ‘Changeling’, and another label regular Point Survey with the phasing dub noise of ‘Print-Through’.\n\nKeener observers may recognise those names already, but perhaps not the new ones here, notably Corbin Cary & Taylor White’s Permutia duo, secreting the fine lather chords and sandman bassline of ‘p1.2’, or HPIN with the early SND-style puckered glitch of ‘Remote’, Uos’ washed-out textures on Uos in ‘Uos Jelly’, and dreamily poised dub waltz of ‘Speedwalker’ by a.m.p & b.p.p.",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "Black Fire Dream",
      "artist": "aisie",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/black-fire-dream",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "techno / house",
      "excerpt": "Enigmatic audity Aisie returns five years on from a strange, overlooked debut with a new suite of compressed atmospheres highly tipped FFO False Aralia, Eliza B.C., Thought Broadcast, Civilistjävel!, Hazyville-era Actress. ‘Black Fire Dream’ picks up from where 2021’s ‘Halcyon Gang Poet’ left us in a surreal, uncanny valley state of mind. The seven part, 30 minute mini-LP continues to fascinate with its cyborganic nature and dreamy otherworldliness, luring down gauzily textured, fractal wormhole",
      "body": "Enigmatic audity Aisie returns five years on from a strange, overlooked debut with a new suite of compressed atmospheres highly tipped FFO False Aralia, Eliza B.C., Thought Broadcast, Civilistjävel!, Hazyville-era Actress.\n\n‘Black Fire Dream’ picks up from where 2021’s ‘Halcyon Gang Poet’ left us in a surreal, uncanny valley state of mind. The seven part, 30 minute mini-LP continues to fascinate with its cyborganic nature and dreamy otherworldliness, luring down gauzily textured, fractal wormholes where samples of “obscure educational science shows, ghost station radio transmissions, vinyl record detritus and blown-out microscopic field recordings” are gently reanimated and transmuted with a poetic sorcery. \n\nThe whole thing feels as though it were conjuured without human touch, like the inner thoughts of an AI or machines autonomously air-syncing and executing their functions in private. With incremental stealth it breezes by in a hypnagogic haze, half-heard melodies sprouting and dissolving into the aether as granular rhythms buckle and trickle. Eyes will likely be at half mast by the end of the A-side, all the best to receive the B-side’s suggestive, illusive shadowplay of smoke and mirrors refraction and a final slope off into something like a chopped and screwed echo of Topdown Dialectic.",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
