      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "jazz / fusion",
      "excerpt": "Coltrane’s invigorating ’66 spiritual free jazz salvo - the follow-up to ‘A Love Supreme’ (1965) - is unleashed from the Verve Vault, spotlighting his classic line-up tearing out on templates set by Ornette Coleman years prior, along with more reserved moments of beauty. An evergreen.. \"Following the genre-redefining revelations of A Love Supreme in 1965, John Coltrane began a dramatic shift toward spiritual free jazz, abandoning familiar forms in favour of a more abstract sonic palette and bold",
      "body": "Coltrane’s invigorating ’66 spiritual free jazz salvo - the follow-up to ‘A Love Supreme’ (1965) - is unleashed from the Verve Vault, spotlighting his classic line-up tearing out on templates set by Ornette Coleman years prior, along with more reserved moments of beauty. An evergreen..\n\n\"Following the genre-redefining revelations of A Love Supreme in 1965, John Coltrane began a dramatic shift toward spiritual free jazz, abandoning familiar forms in favour of a more abstract sonic palette and bold questions he'd spend the rest of his life and career pursuing. Meditations, released by Impulse! in 1966, continues that emotional throughline while retaining, for the last time in full, the classic quartet that propelled Trane to greatness: pianist McCoy Tyner, bassist Jimmy Garrison and drummer Elvin Jones. (They're further augmented by Pharoah Sanders on tenor sax and additional drummer Rashied Ali.) Meditations pushes Coltrane’s spiritual jazz into heightened realms of energy and abstraction — a powerful document of transformation, intensity, and devotion in Coltrane’s recorded legacy.\"",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "Mount Analogue",
      "artist": "Bill Laswell + P.ST",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/mount-analogue-3ab98de2-dbb7-4806-b689-a07575fd27db",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "electronic",
      "excerpt": "Described as a \"musical poem\", 'Mount Analogue' is a lengthy meditation on the works of avant-garde poet and writer René Daumal that's passed from Bill Laswell and P.St (plus an ensemble featuring Nils Petter Movaer, Anna Clementi, Hideo Yamaki and others) to guitarist Henry Kaiser. 'Mount Analogue' is named after Daumel's most well-known book, the self-styled \"Novel of Symbolically Authentic Non-Euclidean Adventures in Mountain Climbing\" that emerged almost a decade after his early death at jus",
      "body": "Described as a \"musical poem\", 'Mount Analogue' is a lengthy meditation on the works of avant-garde poet and writer René Daumal that's passed from Bill Laswell and P.St (plus an ensemble featuring Nils Petter Movaer, Anna Clementi, Hideo Yamaki and others) to guitarist Henry Kaiser.\n\n'Mount Analogue' is named after Daumel's most well-known book, the self-styled \"Novel of Symbolically Authentic Non-Euclidean Adventures in Mountain Climbing\" that emerged almost a decade after his early death at just 36 in 1944. That text is excerpted here on the album-length title composition, that Czech experimental sort P.ST leads on electronics alongside Laswell, Kaiser, vocalists Clementi and Percy Howard, percussionist Yamaki, cornet player Graham Haynes, violinist Dorian Cheah, Keyboardist Peter Apfelbaum and Molvaer on trumpet. It was P.St who came up with the concept in the first place and his direction helps rein in such a wide spread of contributors; from the beginning, there's a sense of calm that's rarely ruptured. Washing pebbles are augmented by instrumental washes and a deep voice reading Daumal's words in English. \"Seeing that I am nothing, I desire to become. Desiring to become, I live.\" reads Howard over Kaiser's tangled plucks. But it's Italian-Swedish singer Clementi's part that really takes this one to the next level, bounding acrobatically over the group's wash of instrumentation to paint in brighter colors before jazzy improvisations take root.\n\nThe second disc is handled exclusively by improv legend Kaiser, who spends almost an hour pondering Alejandro Jodorowsky's 'The Holy Mountain', a film that was directly inspired by Daumal's text, on the absorbing 'Jordorowsky's Peradam', before splitting off with a set of shorter solo jams. And on the digital version, P.St turns in an album length remix of the title track that's almost as good as the original, amping up the noise and the chaos without losing hold of the track's poetic cadence.",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "Architextures 1 -2 -3",
      "artist": "AKUFEN",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/architextures-1-2-3",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "techno / house",
      "excerpt": "Necessary reissue of Marc Leclair’s immaculate Y2K micro-house/dub-house 12” as Akufen, dispensed by Low End Activist’s guess-again BRUK sibling to Sneaker Social Club - huge RIYL Maurizio, Studio 1, Mike Huckaby. ‘Architextures 1 -2 -3’ is a sought-after slice of hypnotic house by a noted pioneer of the micro-house movement that emerged in the late ‘90s. Its reissue arrives in the wake of a re-up for Marc Leclair’s (aka Akufen) sole solo album ‘Musique Pour 3 Femmes Enceintes’ (2005) with a str",
      "body": "Necessary reissue of Marc Leclair’s immaculate Y2K micro-house/dub-house 12” as Akufen, dispensed by Low End Activist’s guess-again BRUK sibling to Sneaker Social Club - huge RIYL Maurizio, Studio 1, Mike Huckaby.\n\n‘Architextures 1 -2 -3’ is a sought-after slice of hypnotic house by a noted pioneer of the micro-house movement that emerged in the late ‘90s. Its reissue arrives in the wake of a re-up for Marc Leclair’s (aka Akufen) sole solo album ‘Musique Pour 3 Femmes Enceintes’ (2005) with a strong reminder of his pivotal role in dressing house music down to fundamentals around the millennium, as deployed in Richie Hawtin mixes and praised for its exquisitely efficient, effortless, hiccuping funk.\n\nIt’s really all about the  A-side’s ‘Architexture 1’, a pendulous 127BPM roller inflected with chef’s kiss dub chords and frisky drums, on one of the smoothest, deepest basslines since ‘M5’. There’s a good reason why it’s been fetching triple figures on 2nd hand markets, so BRUK are doing the Lord’s work with this reissue, which also includes the slower, sub-heavier swivel of its Pt. 2, and more signature, strutting clip of his tight sampling tekkerz on Pt. 3.\n\nTIP!",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "Anda Jaleo / Perlas",
      "artist": "JOSEPHINE FOSTER & THE VICTOR HERRERO BAND",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/anda-jaleo-pearlas",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "folk / roots",
      "excerpt": "Josephine Foster and The Victor Herrero Band release \"Anda Jaleo / Pearlas\" via Fire Records. \"Anda Jaleo was originally released in 2010. Federico Garcia Lorca's popular folk song collection \"Las Canciones Populares Espanolas\" was banned under Franco's dictatorship and today the music survives but marginally within the Spanish sub-conscious. Taking their cue from Lorca and La Argentinita's infectious 1931 recording of the songs, Josephine Foster and her partner Spanish musician Victor Herrero a",
      "body": "Josephine Foster and The Victor Herrero Band release \"Anda Jaleo / Pearlas\" via Fire Records.\n\n\"Anda Jaleo was originally released in 2010. Federico Garcia Lorca's popular folk song collection \"Las Canciones Populares Espanolas\" was banned under Franco's dictatorship and today the music survives but marginally within the Spanish sub-conscious. Taking their cue from Lorca and La Argentinita's infectious 1931 recording of the songs, Josephine Foster and her partner Spanish musician Victor Herrero arranged the poetically rich collection for their acoustic band, formed while living in the Grenadine Sierra. Anda Jaleo is the band's live recording of \"Las Canciones\"; a visceral celebration of the persistence of popular anonymous song. This new edition includes an additional track not featured on the original release, an interpretation of ‘Sones de Asturias’. La colección de \"Canciones Populares Españolas\" recopiladas y armonizadas por Federico García Lorca fue censurada en tiempos de Franco, y hoy en día la música sobrevive aunque de una manera vaga en el subconsciente del pueblo español. Inspirados por la contagiosa grabación de las canciones de Lorca y La Argentinita de 1931, Josephine Foster y su compañero el músico español Víctor Herrero han arreglado esta poética y rica colección para su banda acústica , formada mientras vivían en la sierra de Granada. Anda Jaleo es la grabación en directo de su versión de \"Las Canciones\"; una celebración visceral de la canción popular anónima y su persistencia. Following from Anda Jaleo, Josephine Foster and the Victor Herrero Band created a superb follow-up entitled Perlas (Pearls). It is a jewel of a collection, with songs and poems selected by Josephine herself, gathered from dusty old scores and brought vividly to the present with warm performances full of flesh-and-blood emotion. Made with a variety of stringed instruments and simple percussion, the songs were recorded live in the studio on to analogue tape by Paco Loco in Puerto de Santa Maria, Spain. Foster breathes new life into timeless traditional melodies, drawing from the Spanish-folk traditions of Castile, the Basque, Santander and the Costa Brava.\"",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "Cuisine",
      "artist": "SEVERED HEADS",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/cuisine",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "industrial / wave / electro",
      "excerpt": "Dark Entries pursue prevailing interests in early ‘90s industrial club with 1st vinyl reissue of Severed Heads ’91 LP, framing Australia’s electronic dance pioneers resembling a down under New Order, early Lassigue Bendthaus or C&C in their charmingly melodic synth, EBM and techno-pop arrangements, replete with previously unheard demos and alt. mixes. “Severed Heads reattach themselves to Dark Entries for an expanded reissue of their 1991 opus Cuisine (With Piscatorial). As originary Aussie indu",
      "body": "Dark Entries pursue prevailing interests in early ‘90s industrial club with 1st vinyl reissue of Severed Heads ’91 LP, framing Australia’s electronic dance pioneers resembling a down under New Order, early Lassigue Bendthaus or C&C in their charmingly melodic synth, EBM and techno-pop arrangements, replete with previously unheard demos and alt. mixes.\n\n“Severed Heads reattach themselves to Dark Entries for an expanded reissue of their 1991 opus Cuisine (With Piscatorial). As originary Aussie industrial legends – although founder Tom Ellard would balk at being branded as such – Severed Heads shaped the continental subcultural sound with their kitchen electronics, chaotic tape loops, and infectious nursery-rhyme-esque melodies. Cuisine (With Piscatorial) was the long-running project’s ninth album, and is a commentary on the state of music. \n\nEllard explains: “The whole food joke is really about what music’s about and how disposable it is; people have records like they have cups of coffee.” The album also presents a turn away from the dancefloor formalism of the era, which Ellard dismissed as already sufficiently explored. Cuisine brings us punchy pop kernels of the prime Heads variety, all clocking in around three minutes. Cuts like “Pilot in Hell” and “Ugly Twenties” rank among the band’s best through their deadly skewering of synth pop tropes. \n\nBut the album also offers us a Piscatorial section, where Ellard felt free to “go fishing for ideas.” Here we get a taste of the project’s demented cut-up sensibilities, like on the “Quest for Oom Pa Pa” suite, where vintage jazz records are collaged into an angular nightmare. This double-LP reissue is the first time that Cuisine (With Piscatorial) will appear on vinyl, with a previously unreleased early version of “Seven of Oceans.” Also included is a 6-page booklet with liner notes, lyrics, and press clippings.”",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "Anda Jaleo",
      "artist": "JOSEPHINE FOSTER & THE VICTOR HERRERO BAND",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/anda-jaleo-5c261588-9154-4ad1-8575-b88cc66beb48",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "folk / roots",
      "excerpt": "Josephine Foster and the Victor Herrero Band release \"Anda Jaleo\" via Fire Records. \"A live recording of “Las Canciones”; a visceral celebration of the persistence of popular anonymous song based on the work of legendary socialist poet Federico García Lorca, a Granada born literary pioneer. Featuring songs from his 1931 collection of mysteriously beautiful flamenco tunes. A poetically rich collection created by Foster and Herrero for their acoustic band, formed while living in the Grenadine Sier",
      "body": "Josephine Foster and the Victor Herrero Band release \"Anda Jaleo\" via Fire Records.\n\n\"A live recording of “Las Canciones”; a visceral celebration of the persistence of popular anonymous song based on the work of legendary socialist poet Federico García Lorca, a Granada born literary pioneer. Featuring songs from his 1931 collection of mysteriously beautiful flamenco tunes. A poetically rich collection created by Foster and Herrero for their acoustic band, formed while living in the Grenadine Sierra. “Foster’s vocals, met by husband Herrero’s frantic and raw gypsy-band orchestration, demonstrates the sense of urgency in the music’s message well and carries ‘Anda Jaleo’ to an elevated state.” The Line Of Best Fit... “The alt-folk fixture returns to more traditional material.” Pitchfork.\" \"",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "It Will Take Forever",
      "artist": "Jad Atoui",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/it-will-take-forever",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "electronic",
      "excerpt": "Beirut-based sound artist and veteran improviser Jad Atoui captures his country's current instability on his latest full-length, performing live in situ with his modular rig. Ostensibly a noise record, it's inspired by Atoui's early club experiences, where he twigged the physicality of sound for the first time. Here, he uses the same properties to provoke very different responses, layering distorted waves of sound on 'Pressure Dream' that might as well be collapsing buildings. And by recording t",
      "body": "Beirut-based sound artist and veteran improviser Jad Atoui captures his country's current instability on his latest full-length, performing live in situ with his modular rig.\n\nOstensibly a noise record, it's inspired by Atoui's early club experiences, where he twigged the physicality of sound for the first time. Here, he uses the same properties to provoke very different responses, layering distorted waves of sound on 'Pressure Dream' that might as well be collapsing buildings. And by recording the material live, there's a distinct human touch that's often missing from this kind of material. Atoui is able to work instinctively, reacting to the sound in the room on the outstanding 'Reaching Heart' as glassy drones bend to corroded rhythmic interjections. \n\nThere's even a glimmer of hope; the gorgeous 'Blue Moon Red Cloud' is a break from stuttering beats and searing noise that hits like an oasis in the desert, lifted by Atoui's freeform melodies and delirious FM chimes.",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "Perlas",
      "artist": "JOSEPHINE FOSTER & THE VICTOR HERRERO BAND",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/perlas-bb0d4cd8-7ae3-438d-a22b-ee3979782c05",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "folk / roots",
      "excerpt": "Josephine Foster and the Victor Herrero Band release \"Perlas\" via Fire Records. \"Their follow up to the acclaimed ‘Anda Jaleo’. A document of Josephine Foster's magical partnership with Victor Herrero breathing new life into timeless traditional melodies, drawing from the Spanish-folk traditions of Castile, the Basque, Santander and the Costa Brava. ‘Perlas’ is debonair, contemporary and redolent of that old seductive charge.” The Wire. Elemental themes of love bind the collection together, with",
      "body": "Josephine Foster and the Victor Herrero Band release \"Perlas\" via Fire Records.\n\n\"Their follow up to the acclaimed ‘Anda Jaleo’. A document of Josephine Foster's magical partnership with Victor Herrero breathing new life into timeless traditional melodies, drawing from the Spanish-folk traditions of Castile, the Basque, Santander and the Costa Brava. ‘Perlas’ is debonair, contemporary and redolent of that old seductive charge.” The Wire. Elemental themes of love bind the collection together, with a melancholy joy that casts a shadow of desire and loss. “The alt- folk fixture returns to more traditional material.” Pitchfork.\"",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
    {
      "album": "Never Say When",
