    {
      "album": "Pills 'n' Thrills and Bellyaches",
      "artist": "Happy Mondays",
      "score": null,
      "url": "https://boomkat.com/products/pills-n-thrills-and-bellyaches",
      "source": "Boomkat",
      "pub_date": "2026-08-20",
      "tags": "indie / alternative",
      "excerpt": "Happy Mondays’ \"Pills ‘n’ Thrills and Bellyaches\", originally released in 1990. \"Pills 'n' Thrills and Bellyaches stands as a key document of the Madchester era, fusing indie rock with acid house rhythms and loose-limbed funk. Packed with defining cuts like ‘Step On’ and ‘Kinky Afro’, it captured the hedonistic pulse of dancefloors and Northern nightlife while pushing British alternative music into new territory. Equal parts swagger and groove, the album’s genre-blurring approach helped shape th",
      "body": "Happy Mondays’ \"Pills ‘n’ Thrills and Bellyaches\", originally released in 1990.\n\n\"Pills 'n' Thrills and Bellyaches stands as a key document of the Madchester era, fusing indie rock with acid house rhythms and loose-limbed funk. Packed with defining cuts like ‘Step On’ and ‘Kinky Afro’, it captured the hedonistic pulse of dancefloors and Northern nightlife while pushing British alternative music into new territory.\n\nEqual parts swagger and groove, the album’s genre-blurring approach helped shape the sound of the early ’90s and continues to echo through modern indie and electronic scenes. Remastered from the original Factory Records tapes and accompanied by new liner notes from James Brown, it remains a vivid snapshot of a scene at full tilt.\"",
      "site_id": "boomkat",
      "crawl_status": "success",
      "type": "feature"
    },
